{
  "id": "m4l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Índices, troceado y formato",
    "en": "Indexing, slicing and formatting"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Acceder a partes del texto"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una cadena es una **secuencia** de caracteres. `texto[i]` da un carácter (índice desde 0; los negativos cuentan desde el final). `len(texto)` da su longitud."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"Python\"",
          "print(s[0], s[-1])",
          "print(len(s))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "P n",
          "6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Troceado (slicing)"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`texto[inicio:fin]` devuelve un trozo (sin incluir `fin`). Puedes omitir extremos y usar un paso: `texto[::-1]` invierte la cadena."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"Python\"",
          "print(s[0:3])",
          "print(s[2:])",
          "print(s[::-1])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Pyt",
          "thon",
          "nohtyP"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Formato con f-strings"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Dentro de una f-string puedes dar formato: `{valor:.2f}` con 2 decimales; `{n:>5}` alinea a la derecha en 5 huecos."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "pi = 3.14159",
          "print(f\"{pi:.2f}\")",
          "print(f\"{42:>5}\")"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3.14",
          "   42"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "El troceado **nunca** da error por pasarte de rango: `s[0:100]` simplemente devuelve hasta el final."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Accessing parts of text"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A string is a **sequence** of characters. `text[i]` gives one character (index from 0; negatives count from the end). `len(text)` gives its length."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"Python\"",
          "print(s[0], s[-1])",
          "print(len(s))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "P n",
          "6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Slicing"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`text[start:end]` returns a slice (excluding `end`). You can omit ends and use a step: `text[::-1]` reverses the string."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"Python\"",
          "print(s[0:3])",
          "print(s[2:])",
          "print(s[::-1])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Pyt",
          "thon",
          "nohtyP"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Formatting with f-strings"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Inside an f-string you can format: `{value:.2f}` with 2 decimals; `{n:>5}` right-aligns within 5 slots."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "pi = 3.14159",
          "print(f\"{pi:.2f}\")",
          "print(f\"{42:>5}\")"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3.14",
          "   42"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Slicing **never** errors out of range: `s[0:100]` simply returns up to the end."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m4l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `invertir_texto(s)` que devuelva la cadena al revés (usa el troceado `[::-1]`).",
        "en": "Define `invertir_texto(s)` returning the reversed string (use slicing `[::-1]`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def invertir_texto(s):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def invertir_texto(s):",
        "    return s[::-1]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "s[::-1] recorre la cadena al revés."
        ],
        "en": [
          "s[::-1] walks the string backwards."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "invertir_texto",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "abc"
              ],
              "expected": "cba"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                ""
              ],
              "expected": ""
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "Python"
              ],
              "expected": "nohtyP"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m4l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `truncar(s, n)`: si `s` tiene más de `n` caracteres, devuelve los primeros `n` y añade `…` al final; si no, devuelve `s` tal cual.",
        "en": "Define `truncar(s, n)`: if `s` has more than `n` characters, return the first `n` plus `…`; otherwise return `s` unchanged."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def truncar(s, n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def truncar(s, n):",
        "    if len(s) > n:",
        "        return s[:n] + \"…\"",
        "    return s"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Compara len(s) con n.",
          "s[:n] son los primeros n caracteres."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Compare len(s) with n.",
          "s[:n] is the first n characters."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "truncar",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "Hola mundo",
                4
              ],
              "expected": "Hola…"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "Hi",
                5
              ],
              "expected": "Hi"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "abcde",
                5
              ],
              "expected": "abcde"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}